<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<%- include('partials/html-head', { extraCss: '/api.css' }); -%>

	<body>
		<div id="app" class="wrap" v-cloak>
			<%- include('partials/header', { heading: 'API' }); -%>

			<section class="api-intro">
				<p>
					Every endpoint below authenticates with an API key. Create one under
					<a href="/settings">Settings</a> &rarr; API Keys and send it as the <code>x-api-key</code> header. No cookies
					and no login step, so a plain <code>curl</code> works.
				</p>
				<p>All responses are JSON.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="endpoint">
				<h2><span class="method">POST</span> <code>/api/push</code></h2>
				<p>Send a push notification to one or more users.</p>

				<h3>Parameters</h3>
				<dl class="params">
					<dt>text <span class="tag">body, required</span></dt>
					<dd>
						The message to send. Anything beyond 160 characters is trimmed off. You always receive the push
						yourself. Add <code>@mention</code>s to send it to others too <code>Eg: @alice @bob deploy finished</code>.
						A mentioned user only receives the push if they have added you to their allowed users, or have turned on
						"Allow anyone to send me push". Mentioned users who have not are skipped.
						Use <code>@all</code> to send it to everyone who has added you to their allowed users.
					</dd>
				</dl>

				<h3>Example</h3>
				<pre class="code-block">
curl -X POST https://pushie.net/api/push \
  -H "x-api-key: $PUSHIE_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"text": "Deployment finished on production"}'</pre
				>

				<h3>Response</h3>
				<pre class="code-block response">
{
  "message": "Push sent",
  "to": ["alice"],
  "_id": "68bd0f3c9a1b4c2d5e6f7a80"
}</pre
				>
				<p class="hint">
					Limited to 25 requests every 5 minutes.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="endpoint">
				<h2><span class="method">GET</span> <code>/api/pull</code></h2>
				<p>List the pushes sent to you, newest first.</p>

				<h3>Parameters</h3>
				<dl class="params">
					<dt>skip <span class="tag">query, optional</span></dt>
					<dd>
						How many pushes to skip. Defaults to <code>0</code>. Each call returns up to 50 pushes.
					</dd>
				</dl>

				<h3>Example</h3>
				<pre class="code-block">
curl "https://pushie.net/api/pull?skip=50" \
  -H "x-api-key: $PUSHIE_API_KEY"</pre
				>

				<h3>Response</h3>
				<pre class="code-block response">
{
  "pushes": [
    {
      "from": "alice",
      "text": "Deployment finished on production",
      "date": "2026-09-07T10:24:11.000Z"
    }
  ]
}</pre
				>
				<p class="hint">Pushes are deleted 24 hours after they are sent, so this only ever returns the last day.</p>
			</section>

			<section class="endpoint">
				<h2>Errors</h2>
				<p>
					Failures come back with a matching status code and a JSON body whose <code>message</code> key holds the error
					message.
				</p>
				<pre class="code-block response">{ "message": "Unauthorized" }</pre>

				<dl class="params">
					<dt>400</dt>
					<dd>The request was invalid, for example <code>text</code> is empty or invalid.</dd>
					<dt>401</dt>
					<dd>The <code>x-api-key</code> header is not a valid API key.</dd>
					<dt>403</dt>
					<dd>A <code>POST</code> was sent without the <code>x-api-key</code> header.</dd>
					<dt>404</dt>
					<dd>No endpoint at that path.</dd>
					<dt>429</dt>
					<dd>You went past a rate limit. The message says how long to wait.</dd>
				</dl>
			</section>
		</div>
		<%- include('partials/footer'); -%>
	</body>
</html>
